     "title": "NMSU Extension, Guide E-215 (high-altitude food preparation): at sea level water boils at 212 °F, each 500-ft increase in altitude causes a drop of about 1 °F in the boiling point; as atmospheric pressure decreases, water boils at lower temperatures; table: rolling boil at 7,500 ft 198 °F",
     "label": {"de": "NMSU Extension", "en": "NMSU Extension"}},
    {"id": "S2", "url": "https://extension.colostate.edu/resource/high-elevation-food-preparation/", "checked_at": "2026-11-01",
